    "result_text": "The build is green. \n\nI implemented `checkDigit` as a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the owner's `customerCode`:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `checkDigit` property (integer 0\u20139) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `checkDigit(Owner)` derivation (standard Luhn over the digits of `customerCode`, `null` when the code is absent) and wired it via `@Mapping(target = \"checkDigit\", ...)` on `toOwnerDto`.\n\nThe full test suite passes (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`), including `coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode`, which recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts the exact returned digit.",
